  READ. A* is the amplitude the pooled instrument needs to see
  a mode. The explicit formula puts a single zero's normalised
  amplitude near 1/|rho|. A ratio far above 1 means the design
  cannot detect a single zero and a successor prereg would be
  underpowered by construction; near or below 1 means it can.
  The unblinded spectrum is deliberately NOT computed here.

